From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: WinZapp <gabarrios2006@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 11:16:52 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] engine: adding someone to a one-to-one call names the device
 that answered, and the device in the call does not ring again

When a companion answered with an <accept> that carries no capability (meowcaller's own, and WhatsApp Web's), the invite roster kept the device of the last <preaccept>, usually the phone. The server then treated the companion really in the call as a device that had not answered: it received the group invite as a new offer, no PIDs and no group key, and this client keyed its group receiver to the phone, so every packet of the companion failed to unprotect.

A <preaccept> that arrives after the answer (a phone woken by a push) no longer replaces the device that answered.

onGroupOffer also replaced the live Call with a ringing one when that invite arrived for a call this device was already in, which rang it again and ended its audio. It now applies the invite as a group update.

Validated: engine_invite_device_test.go (seven tests), go test . green.
---
 engine.go                    |  24 ++++++-
 engine_invite_device.go      |  60 ++++++++++++++++
 engine_invite_device_test.go | 136 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
